 #edb/ref 17592186285429 13194139534387 true] [17592186285424 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534387 true] [17592186285424 1041 "selection" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285424 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285426 13194139534387 true] [17592186285424 1110 #uuid "db898e70-56f9-5772-9f9c-eb4a65e7b37b" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285425 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285425 1111 #uuid "00a27d6b-22c3-579d-b3ec-42f2193f261a" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285426 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285426 1111 #uuid "eb18ed28-75b8-5cb9-9a2d-bcc8cac4816f" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285427 1034 "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285427 1111 #uuid "49ac2e7b-4a68-5a26-a6d2-ec6118fc43cb" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285428 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285428 1111 #uuid "45eb8ebc-8ae6-5592-a165-3375aebf28cf" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285429 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285429 1111 #uuid "6f40633a-bc89-5a92-990b-bf696c8fb8c0" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285430 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285431 13194139534387 true] [17592186285430 1089 "q-106300" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285430 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534387 true] [17592186285430 1100 "Determine the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285430 1113 #uuid "d07f0ee1-8739-5256-bf30-c82b7eeddac5" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285430 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-\\frac{1}{2}) & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(x-\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{1}{25}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+\\frac{1}{2}) & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(y+\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{1}{25}{(y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{25}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{25}{(y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{1}{25}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{25}{(y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is ${(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}=25.$" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285432 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285433 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285434 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285435 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285436 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1041 "selection" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285432 13194139534387 true] [17592186285431 1110 #uuid "11b1e003-da9b-596c-ba40-c91af3644f87" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285432 1034 "{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}=25" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285432 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319