17 #edb/ref 17592186285445 13194139534387 true] [17592186285444 1089 "q-15845" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285444 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534387 true] [17592186285444 1100 "Determine the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285444 1113 #uuid "00d82038-4e0a-5079-b90e-fc5cfcb65e81" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285444 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(x-1) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(y-2) & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-1)^{2}+4(y-2)^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+4(y-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the Cartesian equation of the circle is $(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.$" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285446 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285447 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285448 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285449 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285450 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1041 "selection" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285450 13194139534387 true] [17592186285445 1110 #uuid "fa531025-2766-59b6-959b-7553463ec1fd" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285446 1034 "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285446 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285446 1111 #uuid "3660fd32-70e6-5f4c-bf98-27c86b4daeb6" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285447 1034 "(x+1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285447 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285447 1111 #uuid "fc043568-6dad-5196-961f-1b7fa1355fb3" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285448 1034 "(x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=2" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285448 1111 #uuid "c6658429-805d-5158-878a-b40253eab0a8" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285449 1034 "(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285449 1111 #uuid "894e7701-f050-5718-bfa4-99ccd8b67b43" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285450 1034 "(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285450 1111 #uuid "71a7ab43-9280-5582-8056-6f4de3d648f9" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285452 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285455 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285457 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1089 "q-275313" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1100 "The Cartesian equation of the circle defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$(x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}+(y\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-3}}." 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1113 #uuid "1a9d2783-5a0f-5b83-8cab-893c8a31f08f" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285451 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-2}{6} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{36} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{6} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{36} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{36} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation is $(x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=36.$" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285454 13194139534387 true] [17592186285452 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534387 true] [17592186285452 1041 "field-1" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285452 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285454 13194139534387 true] [17592186285452 1110 #uuid "b8764504-3b49-5c0c-b3d1-5d23409093c4" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285453 1034 "3" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285453 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285453 1111 #uuid "b7625393-d3a6-537a-82c0-4aa906791400" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285454 1034 "2" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285454 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534387 true] [17592186285454 1111 #uuid "f69f25ed-e82b-551c-8aec-f8b85a84a806" 13194139534387 true] [17592186285455 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285456 13194139534387 true] [17592186285455